<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/delaware-beach-dunes.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/delaware-beach-dunes-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/delaware-beach-dunes.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/serving-delaware/">Serving Delaware</a></li><li aria-current="page">Bethany Beach</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">The Quiet Resorts</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Bethany Beach, DE</h1><p class="lede">The heart of Delaware’s “Quiet Resorts,” Bethany Beach and its neighbors — South Bethany, Fenwick Island and Ocean View — mix elevated beach homes, canal-front houses and inland communities.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/start-your-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Sussex County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>The Quiet Resorts</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="local-card"><div><h2 class="local-h">Bethany Beach at a glance</h2><dl class="local-dl"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Sussex County</dd></div><div><dt>Neighborhoods</dt><dd>the ocean blocks of Bethany, South Bethany’s canals, Fenwick Island, Sea Colony, Ocean View and Millville</dd></div><div><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Elevated beach homes, canal-front houses on Little Assawoman Bay, condos and inland planned communities</dd></div></dl></div><div><p class="local-k">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Hurricanes</li><li>Nor’easters</li><li>Coastal flooding</li><li>Wind-driven rain</li><li>Dune erosion</li></ul></div></div>

<h2>The Quiet Resorts and their storms</h2>
<p>Bethany Beach, South Bethany and Fenwick Island sit on a narrow strip between the Atlantic and the inland bays. The 1962 Ash Wednesday Storm caused severe damage here, and Sandy in 2012 damaged dunes and roads near the Indian River Inlet. Insurance appraisal in Bethany Beach is coastal work through and through.</p>
<h2>Elevated and canal-front homes</h2>
<p>Many homes here are raised on pilings, with breakaway walls below. South Bethany’s canal-front homes and properties on Little Assawoman Bay face water from the bay side as well as the ocean. Repair costs for elevated construction, decks, stairs and corrosion-resistant hardware are higher than a generic estimate assumes.</p>
<h2>Wind versus flood</h2>
<p>Coastal storms bring both wind and rising water. Homeowners policies generally cover wind damage, while flood policies cover rising water. We document wind-created openings, wind-driven rain and flood damage separately so each policy can be measured fairly. Our <a href="/claim-worksheets/wind-vs-flood-split-estimator/">wind vs. flood split estimator</a> shows how the allocation changes each payment.</p>
<h2>What we see most</h2>
<ul>
<li>Roof, siding and deck damage after coastal storms</li>
<li>Wind versus flood disputes on elevated homes</li>
<li>Large hurricane-deductible claims</li>
<li>Condo community claims in Sea Colony and elsewhere</li>
<li>Water intrusion in seasonal homes</li>
</ul>

