<h2>Questions from Bethany Beach property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you handle Fenwick Island and Ocean View?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We cover all of the Quiet Resorts and inland Sussex communities like Ocean View, Millville and Selbyville.</p></div></details><details><summary>My elevated home had damage below the living area. Is that covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Coverage for areas below elevated floors is often limited, especially under flood policies. We review both policies before valuing the loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is dune erosion covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Erosion and loss of land are generally not covered by property policies. Damage to the structure itself may be, depending on the cause.</p></div></details></div>
